1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:05,214
This is a front-engine, rear-wheel-drive
car with a five-speed manual gearbox.

2
00:00:07,250 --> 00:00:13,071
Let's look inside, at the parts that turn
burning fuel into turning wheels.

3
00:00:14,250 --> 00:00:16,393
Power starts in the engine.

4
00:00:16,393 --> 00:00:19,393
It flows through the clutch and gearbox,

5
00:00:19,393 --> 00:00:24,107
along the propeller shaft to the
differential at the rear axle,

6
00:00:24,107 --> 00:00:27,786
and out through two driveshafts to the
wheels.

7
00:00:29,250 --> 00:00:30,786
Let's follow it.

8
00:00:32,250 --> 00:00:36,964
The engine is an inline four: four
cylinders in a row,

9
00:00:36,964 --> 00:00:39,357
each with a sliding piston.

10
00:00:40,250 --> 00:00:43,679
Connecting rods link the pistons to the
crankshaft,

11
00:00:43,679 --> 00:00:46,071
turning up-and-down motion into rotation.

12
00:00:47,250 --> 00:00:51,786
Each cylinder repeats a four-stroke cycle
over two crankshaft turns.

13
00:00:53,250 --> 00:00:55,393
Intake: the piston moves down,

14
00:00:55,393 --> 00:00:59,929
drawing air and fuel in through the open
intake valves.

15
00:01:00,250 --> 00:01:05,643
Compression: the intake valves close, and
the rising piston squeezes the mixture.

16
00:01:07,250 --> 00:01:13,500
Power: a spark ignites the mixture, and
the hot gas forces the piston down.

17
00:01:14,250 --> 00:01:20,500
Exhaust: with the exhaust valves open, the
rising piston pushes the burnt gas out.

18
00:01:21,250 --> 00:01:22,964
Camshafts open the valves.

19
00:01:22,964 --> 00:01:28,536
A timing chain drives them from the
crankshaft at exactly half its speed,

20
00:01:28,536 --> 00:01:32,643
because each valve opens only once every
two turns.

21
00:01:33,750 --> 00:01:38,893
Only the power stroke drives the
crankshaft, so the cylinders take turns,

22
00:01:38,893 --> 00:01:45,143
firing in the order one, three, four, two:
a power stroke every half turn.

23
00:01:46,250 --> 00:01:50,536
At the back, a heavy flywheel smooths out
the pulses.

24
00:01:50,536 --> 00:01:54,214
Its face is one half of the clutch.

25
00:01:54,750 --> 00:02:00,750
Between the engine and the gearbox sits
the clutch: the flywheel, a friction disc,

26
00:02:00,750 --> 00:02:04,429
and a pressure plate with a diaphragm
spring.

27
00:02:05,750 --> 00:02:12,429
The disc's hub is splined to the gearbox
input shaft, so they always turn together.

28
00:02:13,250 --> 00:02:14,964
With the pedal up,

29
00:02:14,964 --> 00:02:19,679
the spring clamps the disc between the
pressure plate and flywheel,

30
00:02:19,679 --> 00:02:23,357
so the input shaft turns with the engine.

31
00:02:24,250 --> 00:02:30,250
Press the pedal, and fluid flows from the
master cylinder to the slave cylinder.

32
00:02:30,250 --> 00:02:34,964
It pushes the release fork and bearing
against the spring's fingers.

33
00:02:34,964 --> 00:02:40,786
The spring flexes, the pressure plate
pulls back, and the disc is free.

34
00:02:43,250 --> 00:02:46,679
To pull away, the pedal comes up slowly.

35
00:02:46,679 --> 00:02:50,536
The disc slips between the flywheel and
pressure plate,

36
00:02:50,536 --> 00:02:56,786
speeding up as it passes on torque, until
it matches the engine and locks.

37
00:02:58,250 --> 00:03:00,393
The gearbox has three shafts.

38
00:03:00,393 --> 00:03:05,107
The input shaft, driven by the clutch,
turns the countershaft below.

39
00:03:05,107 --> 00:03:10,500
The output shaft runs out the back, in
line with the input.

40
00:03:11,250 --> 00:03:16,821
The other countershaft gears each mesh
with a gear on the output shaft.

41
00:03:16,821 --> 00:03:21,964
They're always in mesh, but the output
gears spin freely on bearings.

42
00:03:21,964 --> 00:03:27,357
Until one is locked to the shaft, no power
gets through: neutral.

43
00:03:27,750 --> 00:03:29,464
Synchronizers do the locking.

44
00:03:29,464 --> 00:03:35,036
A hub is splined to the shaft, and a
sleeve slides on it.

45
00:03:35,036 --> 00:03:38,464
Each gear carries dog teeth and a cone,

46
00:03:38,464 --> 00:03:42,571
with a brass blocker ring between cone and
sleeve.

47
00:03:43,750 --> 00:03:50,429
Slide the sleeve over the dog teeth, and
the gear is locked to the shaft.

48
00:03:51,250 --> 00:03:54,250
Forks on shift rails move the sleeves.

49
00:03:54,250 --> 00:03:59,643
Moving the lever sideways picks a rail;
forward or back slides it.

50
00:04:01,750 --> 00:04:06,036
In first, the input gear turns the
countershaft more slowly,

51
00:04:06,036 --> 00:04:10,321
and a small countershaft gear drives a
large output gear:

52
00:04:10,321 --> 00:04:15,464
the engine turns about three and a half
times per output-shaft turn.

53
00:04:15,464 --> 00:04:18,893
Fourth locks input to output: one to one.

54
00:04:18,893 --> 00:04:20,857
Fifth is an overdrive.

55
00:04:21,750 --> 00:04:27,571
Reverse adds an idler gear between the
shafts, so the output turns backwards.

56
00:04:29,250 --> 00:04:35,500
Here's a shift from first to second at
three thousand rpm, slowed right down.

57
00:04:36,250 --> 00:04:37,536
One: clutch in.

58
00:04:37,536 --> 00:04:39,500
The engine is disconnected.

59
00:04:41,750 --> 00:04:45,857
Two: the sleeve slides out of first, into
neutral.

60
00:04:47,250 --> 00:04:51,107
Three: the blocker ring's cone presses on
second gear.

61
00:04:51,107 --> 00:04:56,250
Friction slows it, along with the
countershaft, input shaft and clutch disc,

62
00:04:56,250 --> 00:04:59,500
until it matches the output shaft's speed.

63
00:05:01,250 --> 00:05:05,536
Four: speeds matched, the blocker ring
lets the sleeve through,

64
00:05:05,536 --> 00:05:07,929
onto second gear's dog teeth.

65
00:05:09,750 --> 00:05:11,036
Five: clutch out.

66
00:05:11,036 --> 00:05:16,179
The engine is reconnected at about
eighteen hundred rpm: same road speed,

67
00:05:16,179 --> 00:05:17,286
taller gear.

68
00:05:19,250 --> 00:05:24,214
The propeller shaft carries the drive back
to the rear axle.

69
00:05:25,750 --> 00:05:31,321
There, a small pinion drives a large ring
gear: ten teeth against forty-one,

70
00:05:31,321 --> 00:05:38,000
a final drive ratio of 4.1 to 1, turning
the drive through a right angle.

71
00:05:39,750 --> 00:05:43,607
The ring gear is bolted to the
differential case.

72
00:05:43,607 --> 00:05:47,464
Inside, two spider gears mesh with two
side gears,

73
00:05:47,464 --> 00:05:49,857
one splined to each driveshaft.

74
00:05:51,250 --> 00:05:55,536
Going straight, the spider gears don't
spin on their pin.

75
00:05:55,536 --> 00:05:59,214
Everything turns as one, and both wheels
match.

76
00:06:00,250 --> 00:06:05,393
In a turn, the outer wheel travels further
than the inner one.

77
00:06:05,393 --> 00:06:08,821
The spider gears now spin on their pin,

78
00:06:08,821 --> 00:06:12,679
letting one side speed up as the other
slows.

79
00:06:12,679 --> 00:06:16,786
The case turns at the average of the two.

80
00:06:18,250 --> 00:06:22,107
Each driveshaft has a constant-velocity
joint at each end,

81
00:06:22,107 --> 00:06:27,500
because the wheel moves up and down while
the differential stays put.

82
00:06:28,750 --> 00:06:34,750
In the outer joint, six balls run in
grooves between inner and outer races.

83
00:06:34,750 --> 00:06:39,464
A cage holds them in the plane that splits
the angle,

84
00:06:39,464 --> 00:06:43,571
so the wheel turns at exactly the shaft's
speed.

85
00:06:45,250 --> 00:06:47,821
The inner joint can also slide,

86
00:06:47,821 --> 00:06:51,450
as the wheel's distance from the
differential changes.

87
00:06:51,750 --> 00:06:57,571
Finally, the wheel turns, the tire grips
the road, and the car moves.

88
00:06:59,750 --> 00:07:02,143
Let's put it all together.

89
00:07:03,750 --> 00:07:09,143
Clutch up in first, and the engine pulls
to three thousand rpm.

90
00:07:09,750 --> 00:07:16,000
Clutch in, second gear, clutch out: the
revs drop, and the car keeps accelerating.

91
00:07:16,750 --> 00:07:17,857
Then third.

92
00:07:21,750 --> 00:07:25,179
Engine, clutch, gearbox, propeller shaft,
final drive, differential,

93
00:07:25,179 --> 00:07:30,571
and driveshafts: one chain of gears and
shafts, turning fuel into motion.
